From: Androlinzberg maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] libutils: expose borrowed poll state to the host owner loop

Reuse stock MessageQueue and Looper for Java and native input callbacks. The
Wayland owner polls the current epoll descriptor without taking ownership, and
includes native message deadlines alongside Java deadlines. Read the first
envelope under the same lock as sendMessageAtTime, including newly posted work.
Cross-thread posts still use the stock wake path. No Looper state is added.

--- a/libutils/include/utils/Looper.h
+++ b/libutils/include/utils/Looper.h
@@ -416,6 +416,15 @@
      */
     bool isPolling() const;
 
+    // Hosted outer loops borrow this descriptor and combine both queues' deadlines.
+    // Call on the owning thread after pollOnce; never read or close the descriptor.
+    void getHostPollState(int* fd, int* timeoutMillis) {
+        AutoMutex lock(mLock);
+        *fd = mEpollFd.get();
+        *timeoutMillis = mMessageEnvelopes.isEmpty() ? -1 : toMillisecondTimeoutDelay(
+                systemTime(SYSTEM_TIME_MONOTONIC), mMessageEnvelopes.itemAt(0).uptime);
+    }
+
